<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<jcr:root xmlns:jcr="http://www.jcp.org/jcr/1.0"
          xmlns:kes="http://kestros.io/kes/1.0"
          xmlns:mix="http://www.jcp.org/jcr/mix/1.0"
          xmlns:nt="http://www.jcp.org/jcr/nt/1.0"
          xmlns:rep="http://www.jcp.org/jcr/1.0"
          xmlns:sling="http://sling.apache.org/jcr/sling/1.0"
          jcr:primaryType="kes:Page"
>
    <jcr:content
            jcr:description="Some notes after the Blackrock conversion wrapped."
            jcr:mixinTypes="[mix:lockable]"
            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
            jcr:title="Working with an old building is a conversation, not a translation"
            kes:template="/libs/kestros/commons/base-site-template"
            sling:resourceType="kestros/commons/components/kestros-base-page"
    >
        <header
                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                sling:resourceType="kestros/commons/components/inherited-content-area"
        />
        <main
                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                sling:resourceType="kestros/commons/components/content-area"
        >
            <hero
                    inlineVariations="uk-section uk-section-primary"
                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                    sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/section"
            >
                <container
                        inlineVariations="uk-container"
                        jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                        sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/container"
                >
                    <meta
                            inlineVariations="uk-text-meta uk-text-uppercase"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                            text="June 2019. M. Haven."
                    />
                    <heading
                            headingText="Working with an old building is a conversation, not a translation"
                            headingType="h1"
                            inlineVariations="uk-heading-medium"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/heading"
                    />
                    <dek
                            inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                            text="Some notes after the Blackrock conversion wrapped."
                    />
                </container>
            </hero>
            <body
                    inlineVariations="uk-section uk-section-default"
                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                    sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/section"
            >
                <container
                        inlineVariations="uk-container"
                        jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                        sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/container"
                >
                    <p0
                            inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                            text="Blackrock Studio wrapped last month and I have been thinking about what I would tell a younger version of myself about renovation work. There are two traps. The first is to try to hide the existing building under a layer of new material, as if the old structure were something to be corrected. The second is to make too big a deal about the old building, to treat every beam and bolt as a precious object that must be preserved."
                    />
                    <p1
                            inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                            text="The middle path is something like a conversation. The old building has things to say, and so do you. You listen to it for a few weeks before you say anything back. Then you put up a wall where it needs to be, you leave a hoist overhead because it is beautiful, and you let the compromise be visible."
                    />
                    <p2
                            inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                            text="A client once asked me what percentage of an old building we should keep in a renovation. I do not have a number. But the question is wrong. It is not about percentages. It is about which moves pay and which moves do not."
                    />
                </container>
            </body>
        </main>
        <footer
                jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                sling:resourceType="kestros/commons/components/inherited-content-area"
        />
    </jcr:content>
</jcr:root>
